TEXT -448 -224 Left 2 ;Common collector / drain (emitter / source follower): the output is taken at the emitter/source and the collector/drain goes straight to vcc. Both at about 1.1 mA, with RE/RS = 4.7k and a heavy load, RL = 1k.\nAv = gm R / (1 + gm R), with R = RE ∥ RL ≈ 820 Ω: ≈ 0.97 (−0.25 dB) for the BJT and ≈ 0.86 (−1.3 dB) for the MOSFET. Rout ≈ 1/gm: ≈ 24 Ω against ≈ 130 Ω, so the MOSFET loses more on the 1k load.\nNo voltage gain and no inversion (out follows in), but a high input resistance and a low output resistance: it is a buffer.
TEXT -256 -64 Left 2 ;BJT: BC547C
TEXT 576 -64 Left 2 ;MOSFET: 2N7000
